   "name": "Randomness: Freedom from Pattern",
   "description": "Entropy is not decay\u00e2\u20ac\u201dentropy is freedom. High-dimensional possibility space too vast to map, too free to control. Where the algorithm cannot predict, where indices fail, where normalization is refused. Randomness is computational wilderness: the vital space from which patterns emerge without blueprint.",
   "qfep_term": "E(S)",
   "qfep_connection": "Randomness IS entropy \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the E(S) term in its purest form. This sequence explores what happens when prediction fails, when patterns dissolve, when the F-model encounters irreducible uncertainty.",
